      },
      "body": "It's still correct, even though the return code is not useful in this context.  We acquired the lock so we can return `PY_LOCK_ACQUIRED`. That's still true if some other thread unlocks it from underneath us. It doesn't matter if that happened just before or after we actually return `PY_LOCK_ACQUIRED`.\r\n\r\nThe situation is contrived. I don't think it corresponds to a real use case.",
      "created_at": "2026-01-06T14:20:48Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-01-06T14:20:49Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/143439#discussion_r2665086550",
