        "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/colesbury/repos",
        "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/colesbury/events{/privacy}",
        "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/colesbury/received_events",
        "type": "User",
        "user_view_type": "public",
        "site_admin": false
      },
      "body": "The important thing is that there's now way for a caller to distinguish between:\r\n\r\nCase 1:\r\n1) We acquire the lock via handoff\r\n2) Someone else unlocks it in another thread\r\n3) We return `PY_LOCK_ACQUIRED`\r\n4) The caller of `thread.Lock.lock()` continues execution\r\n\r\nCase 2:\r\n1) We acquire the lock via handoff\r\n2) We return `PY_LOCK_ACQUIRED`\r\n3) Someone else unlocks it in another thread\r\n4) The caller of `thread.Lock.lock()` continues execution\r\n",
      "created_at": "2026-01-06T14:22:56Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-01-06T14:22:56Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/143439#discussion_r2665095220",
      "pull_request_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python/cpython/pulls/143439",
